{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Knot.ClausenValueBounds","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Knot.ClausenValueBounds","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.PSeries","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecificLimits.Basic","lean:module:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.abs_VOL_4_1_sub_decimal_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.abs_VOL_4_1_sub_decimal_lt","kind":"theorem","line":203,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/ClausenValueBounds.lean#L203-L220","doc":"**The exact volume meets its decimal carrier**: the transcendental\n`VOL_4_1 = 2·Cl₂(π/3)` and the 30-digit approximation carrier\n`VOL_4_1_decimal` agree within `1/10` — machine-certified, closing the\n\"no formal identity is claimed\" gap at the first decimal.\n(bean qou-44ma) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.abs_Cl_2_pi_div_three_sub_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.abs_Cl_2_pi_div_three_sub_le","kind":"theorem","line":193,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/ClausenValueBounds.lean#L193-L201","doc":"**Certified bound on the Clausen value.** The exact rational-times-`√3`\n24-term partial sum approximates `Cl₂(π/3)` within `1/24`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.sqrt_three_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.sqrt_three_lt","kind":"theorem","line":190,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/ClausenValueBounds.lean#L190-L191","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.sqrt_three_gt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.sqrt_three_gt","kind":"theorem","line":187,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/ClausenValueBounds.lean#L187-L188","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.S24_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.S24_eq","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/ClausenValueBounds.lean#L128-L185","doc":"The 24-term partial sum, exactly: a rational multiple of `√3` by the\nperiod-6 sine pattern `sin(kπ/3) ∈ {√3/2, √3/2, 0, −√3/2, −√3/2, 0}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.tail_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.tail_le","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/ClausenValueBounds.lean#L99-L126","doc":"Crude but certified tail bound: the series tail past 24 terms is at most\n`1/24` in absolute value. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.hasSum_telescope","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.hasSum_telescope","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/ClausenValueBounds.lean#L62-L97","doc":"The telescoping tail series `Σ (1/(i+24) − 1/(i+25))` sums to `1/24`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.summable_cl2Term","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.summable_cl2Term","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/ClausenValueBounds.lean#L58-L60","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.norm_cl2Term_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.norm_cl2Term_le","kind":"theorem","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/ClausenValueBounds.lean#L51-L56","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.summable_one_div_add_one_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.summable_one_div_add_one_sq","kind":"theorem","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/ClausenValueBounds.lean#L41-L49","doc":"Shifted inverse squares are summable. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.cl2_pi3_eq_tsum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.cl2_pi3_eq_tsum","kind":"theorem","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/ClausenValueBounds.lean#L38-L39","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.cl2Term","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.cl2Term","kind":"def","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/ClausenValueBounds.lean#L34-L36","doc":"The `k`-th term of the `Cl₂(π/3)` Fourier series. ","signatureChunk":0}]}